(1862047, 251346, 33845, '<td valign="top">thank you very much Alienyst<br/>It´s great to hear what others think about ones images.<br/>It´s both helpful and interesting to get others point of view.</td>', 'thank you very much AlienystIt´s great to hear what others think about ones images.It´s both helpful and interesting to get others point of view.', '2005-11-13 12:15:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(1862396, 251438, 24962, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club:<br/> <br/>This was your entry in the Transparency II challenge and it fits the brief very well.<br/> <br/>Technical:<br/>Good use of maximum size allowed. Good DOF and focusing. None of the processing or sharpening seems overdone, although the arm of the glasses on the left of the photo seems a bit over bright. The centre of focus is the glasses and so is sharper than the child''s eyes.<br/> <br/>Composition:<br/>A well composed image. The glasses divide the image 50/50 and I don''t quite see the connection of the text with the child, unless it is the words highlighted. It is a clever move to include the child''s eyes in the one frame of the glasses and it looks like the child is actually looking at you.<br/> <br/>Overall:<br/>Not the most original idea but it works. There are some nice touches, the focus is great as is DOF and it is not easy to get a clear shot of a page and through glasses. Nothing has been overdone in the processing stages and your score reflects the opinion of voters. I will watch your future entries. I hope this is helpful and constructive.<br/> <br/>Steve</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club: This was your entry in the Transparency II challenge and it fits the brief very well. Technical:Good use of maximum size allowed. Good DOF and focusing. None of the processing or sharpening seems overdone, although the arm of the glasses on the left of the photo seems a bit over bright. The centre of focus is the glasses and so is sharper than the child''s eyes. Composition:A well composed image. The glasses divide the image 50/50 and I don''t quite see the connection of the text with the child, unless it is the words highlighted. It is a clever move to include the child''s eyes in the one frame of the glasses and it looks like the child is actually looking at you. Overall:Not the most original idea but it works. There are some nice touches, the focus is great as is DOF and it is not easy to get a clear shot of a page and through glasses. Nothing has been overdone in the processing stages and your score reflects the opinion of voters. I will watch your future entries. I hope this is helpful and constructive. Steve', '2005-11-13 16:04:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(1862505, 249981, 36371, '<td valign="top">Ok....fess up! That''s not a drop at all, is it?? It''s glass for sure, but I haven''t figured it out yet.</td>', 'Ok....fess up! That''s not a drop at all, is it?? It''s glass for sure, but I haven''t figured it out yet.', '2005-11-13 17:11:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(1863095, 251423, 42567, '<td valign="top">***Greeting from the Critique Club***<br/> <br/>Lets start by, does this meet the challenge...yes, I think this is a great Transparency picture.  Your exposure time is great, one of the best I''ve ever seen.  The highlight on her chest looks really good.  She is a very pretty model.<br/> <br/>I can''t find anything wrong with the picture.  I think where you lost points with the voters is her head is cut off.  But having her head in the picture you lose the focus on her chest.  I guess it can go both ways.  IMO<br/> <br/>I hope my critique helps.  Great job and a great picture!<br/> <br/>Phillip<br/></td>', '***Greeting from the Critique Club*** Lets start by, does this meet the challenge...yes, I think this is a great Transparency picture.  Your exposure time is great, one of the best I''ve ever seen.  The highlight on her chest looks really good.  She is a very pretty model. I can''t find anything wrong with the picture.  I think where you lost points with the voters is her head is cut off.  But having her head in the picture you lose the focus on her chest.  I guess it can go both ways.  IMO I hope my critique helps.  Great job and a great picture! Phillip', '2005-11-13 20:55:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(1869170, 249920, 3724, '<td valign="top">Very good optical progression.....   I should have scored this one higher.  fyi ...5    Some minor distractions for me include:  disregard for the full frame, - what ever it was or might have been, ie. the obvious tight crop around the subject (it may be traditional but I usually like fullframe); it has, for me a uninteresting commercial (throw some money at it) quality (Imperfections included), Anchor Hocking might use it as a stock image; it''s representative of a slick dpc style that does well, is ment to sell, but usually has no dirt - EddyG is a master of this.  <br/> <br/>Technically excellent.</td>', 'Very good optical progression.....   I should have scored this one higher.  fyi ...5    Some minor distractions for me include:  disregard for the full frame, - what ever it was or might have been, ie. the obvious tight crop around the subject (it may be traditional but I usually like fullframe); it has, for me a uninteresting commercial (throw some money at it) quality (Imperfections included), Anchor Hocking might use it as a stock image; it''s representative of a slick dpc style that does well, is ment to sell, but usually has no dirt - EddyG is a master of this.   Technically excellent.', '2005-11-15 16:15:54.000000', NULL, 0),
