(1905958, 251488, 43115, '<td valign="top">I wouldn''t worry too much about your place... this was a rather high scoring challenge overall.  A 4.6 isn''t bad at all for a first entry.  It takes a little while to figure out what works here.<br/> <br/>I think it''s a good picture.  Not great, definatley not horrible.<br/> <br/>My argument for getting rid of the motion blur, either with a crop, or with faster shutter speed, is that it detracts from the point of the photo, which is the transparency of the first building.  You don''t want people being distracted by the cars.  If you had cropped that out then you could have metered the exposure for the building and lightened the whole thing up a little bit.<br/> <br/>Just my $.02  :)</td>', 'I wouldn''t worry too much about your place... this was a rather high scoring challenge overall.  A 4.6 isn''t bad at all for a first entry.  It takes a little while to figure out what works here. I think it''s a good picture.  Not great, definatley not horrible. My argument for getting rid of the motion blur, either with a crop, or with faster shutter speed, is that it detracts from the point of the photo, which is the transparency of the first building.  You don''t want people being distracted by the cars.  If you had cropped that out then you could have metered the exposure for the building and lightened the whole thing up a little bit. Just my $.02  :)', '2005-11-29 23:47:55.000000', NULL, 0),
